("T29", "How much is the CPL assessment fee per credit hour? And if my professor suspects me of academic dishonesty, what is the first step that happens?",
 "Credit for Prior Learning institutional assessments cost $40 per credit hour (for both exams and portfolios). For suspected academic dishonesty, the first step is that the professor meets the student and presents a written outline of the alleged dishonesty, the evidence supporting the charge, and the penalty.", A,
 "REDRAW S5 (GC2627-0071 / GC2627-0085 not naturally linked). Spare S5 is only loosely linked: compound question.", ""),
("T30", "Which laws the ATU is following for non-discrimination, and whom I should contact for the sexual misconduct complaints? Please give the contact details also.",
 "ATU complies with laws including Title VI and Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Sections 503 and 504 of the Rehabilitation Act, the Age Discrimination Act and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, among others. Complaints about sex (gender) discrimination or sexual misconduct may be made to the ATU Title IX Coordinator, Amy Pennington, apennington@atu.edu, 479-968-0407.", A, "", ""),
("T31", "Under which federal law the ATU Alcohol and Other Drugs policy is required? And how I should submit a complaint to Student Affairs, in writing or verbally, and whom to contact for help?",
 "The Alcohol and Other Drugs policy is required under the Drug-Free Schools and Communities Act. Complaints should be submitted in writing to the appropriate office or department; concerns sent to Student Affairs are referred to the responsible area, and for assistance one can contact the Associate Dean for Student Conduct.", A,
 "REDRAW S6 (SH2026-0271 / SH2026-0231 not naturally linked)", ""),
("T32", "I am a senior in my bachelor's. How many graduate hours I can take with special permission now? And for non-degree graduate admission, how many hours can be applied later to a degree program?",
 "An undergraduate senior may, with special permission from the Dean of Graduate College, enroll in no more than six (6) hours of graduate coursework (total course load not above 15 hours in fall/spring, 6 in summer; 3.00 cumulative GPA needed). For non-degree graduate students, a maximum of twelve (12) graduate hours earned in non-degree status may apply to a degree program.", A, "", ""),
("T33", "I changed my name after marriage. Which office I should go and which form to submit? And the same office can give my official transcript also or not?",
 "Submit a completed Name Change form to the Registrar's Office. The Office of the Registrar also provides official academic transcripts (and manages academic records, registration and graduation-related processes).", A, "", ""),
("T34", "Between the Master of Science in Nursing and the Master of Science in Health Informatics, what is the focus of each program? Kindly explain both.",
 "The MS in Nursing provides advanced study for nurses in the area of administration and emergency management. The MS in Health Informatics (MSHI) is a specialized program serving workforce needs in health information technology, combining health care delivery concepts with information technology in a multidisciplinary curriculum.", A, "", ""),

